Question: Would you use a StatelessWidget or StatefulWidget for this screen? Justify your choice clearly and explain the exact mechanism 
by which calling setState() causes Flutter to re-draw only the affected portion of the widget tree.

Answer:
I would use a StatefulWidget because the cart screen's quantity and total price change when the user taps the '+' or '–' buttons.

When setState() is called Flutter marks the corresponding widget as needing a rebuild. Flutter calls build() again and updates the 
necessary parts of the widget tree while reusing unchanged elements. This allows the quantity and total price to update immediately 
without navigating away from the screen.
